{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Editor Button Operator Binding.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Editor Button Operator Binding.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender editor button operator binding blender editor button operator binding","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Editor Button Operator Binding.md","fileName":"Blender Editor Button Operator Binding.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Editor Button Operator Binding","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Editor Construction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Editor Construction","Blender UI Button","Blender Operator Type Structure","Blender Operator Poll Method","Blender Operator Exec Callback","Blender Custom SpaceLink Type","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Editor Button Operator Binding.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Editor Button Operator Binding.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender editor button operator binding blender editor button operator binding","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Editor Button Operator Binding.md","fileName":"Blender Editor Button Operator Binding.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Editor Button Operator Binding","heading":"Blender Editor Button Operator Binding","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A core editor can connect a C-created [[Blender UI Button]] to an operation by finding the registered [[Blender Operator Type Structure]] by identifier and assigning that type to the button. The link is established while the header region is drawn.\n\nWhen the user clicks the button, Blender calls the operation's [[Blender Operator Poll Method]] and then its [[Blender Operator Exec Callback]]. The tutorial's callback